deps-restorer: a reader never sees a hoisted package half-removed or half-imported (homescoop#1128)

stage_and_swap removed the old package tree before renaming the staged
one into place, so for the whole recursive delete (long on OPFS) a
reader of node_modules/<pkg> saw it empty out file by file, then not
there. Move the old tree aside with one rename, rename the staged tree
in, then delete the old one. A brand-new package (import_absent_dir, not
shared) is populated in a private sibling and renamed into place too.
Between the two renames the directory is briefly absent; there's no
portable atomic exchange of non-empty directories. The upstream test
for a failing remove_dir_all (RemoveExisting) becomes one that an
unremovable old tree no longer fails the swap.

